ation and likely improves speed significantly. We can also try `#pragma omp for schedule(static)` on first loop but with `simd`? Not sure.\n\nMaybe we can use `reduction(max:mxSum)` with `schedule(static, 1)`? Previous experiment showed worse. So keep static default.\n\nAnother idea: Use `collapse(2)` on the second loop if we restructure to parallelize over both r and c without sliding dependency? Could compute each submatrix sum independently using colPref in O(s) or O(1)? With colPref, a submatrix sum can be computed as sum_{c=0}^{s-1} (colPref[bottom][r+c] - ...). That's O(s) per submatrix. If we parallelize over all (n-s+1)^2 submatrices with reduction max, each iteration does s work; total O((n-s+1)^2 * s), which could be worse than sliding O((n-s+1)*n). But maybe better parallelism? Not likely.\n\nSo raw pointer allocation is a good candidate. Let's also consider using `std::unique_ptr` with custom deleter to avoid manual delete, but new/delete fine.\n\nLet's write the code:\n\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nclass FastScanner {\npublic:\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    int idx, size;\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return 0;\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n    int nextInt() {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n        bool neg = false;\n        if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getChar(); }\n        int x = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        return neg ? -x : x;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    // Use raw pointers to avoid zero-initialization overhead of std::vector\n    int* mat = new int[n * n];\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            mat[i*n + j] = fs.nextInt();\n\n    long long* colPref = new long long[n * n];\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            long long running = 0;\n            int* colBase = mat + j; // stride n, but we'll use index math\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n                running += mat[i*n + j];\n                colPref[i*n + j] = running;\n            }\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n        for (int r = 0; r <= n - s; ++r) {\n            int bottom = r + s - 1;\n            int topMinusOne = r - 1;\n            long long cur = 0;\n            const int bottomBase = bottom * n;\n            const int topBase = (topMinusOne >= 0 ? topMinusOne * n : 0);\n            for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) {\n                long long seg = colPref[bottomBase + c] - (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topBase + c] : 0);\n                cur += seg;\n            }\n            if (cur > mxSum) mxSum = cur;\n\n            for (int c = 1; c <= n - s; ++c) {\n                int outCol = c - 1;\n                int inCol = c + s - 1;\n                long long segOut = colPref[bottomBase + outCol] - (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topBase + outCol] : 0);\n                long long segIn = colPref[bottomBase + inCol] - (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topBase + inCol] : 0);\n                cur += segIn - segOut;\n                if (cur > mxSum) mxSum = cur;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)mxSum);\n\n    delete[] mat;\n    delete[] colPref;\n}\n```\n\nWe added bottomBase and topBase to avoid repeated multiplication. Also removed <vector> include.\n\nThis should be correct. The main change is raw pointers ins